Insuperlex is one of [[Aut]]'s siblings, called the Mountain. He is the obstacle set before a hero, and he clashes with [[Divinity/The Narrative/Menhir|the Menhir]] the same way [[Aut]] clashes with [[Divinity/The Narrative/Renge|Renge]]. Those who serve him get nothing but challenges, and of all the narrative siblings he is held to be the worst master. He has lately taken an interest in the Party's pilgrimage, and the servants of his siblings now assume all five of them are watching the voyage.

The Menhir he clashed with is dead, killed by the Party with the weapon the Menhir itself had put in their hands, and the counterpart that checked him is gone.
